<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index rallies 2.17 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index rallies 2.17 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index rose 1.65 points, 2.17 percent, to 77.82 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index rose 23.54 pts to a provisional 3,287.66.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 20.27 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
